menu "SPI NAND FatFs throughput example configuration"

    config EXAMPLE_TEST_TRIES
        int "Repeat count per (phase, chunk size) test cell"
        default 3
        range 1 5
        help
            Number of write+read passes per (phase, chunk size) cell,
            reported as mean/min/max throughput.

    config EXAMPLE_PRECONDITION_ENABLE
        bool "Precondition (age) the filesystem before measuring throughput"
        default y
        help
            Before the timed phases, write a fill file covering
            EXAMPLE_PRECONDITION_FILL_PERCENT of the volume's free space and
            keep it. The FTL then holds that much live data, so the timed
            phases run on a partly full device where garbage collection has
            to relocate live pages, instead of on a fresh chip.

    config EXAMPLE_PRECONDITION_FILL_PERCENT
        int "Percent of free space to precondition"
        depends on EXAMPLE_PRECONDITION_ENABLE
        default 20
        range 10 80
        help
            Size of the fill file as a percentage of the free space right
            after mount. The timed phases use the remaining space.

endmenu
